# start Validation Reply Form
_vrf_PLAT971_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.78Ang From I3              5.26 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density near the heavy atoms, which is around 10% of the electron density of I3. It is not from unaccounted atom types. Due to the phase transition and the layered nature of the structure, small densities of stacking faults or other unresolved disorder may lead to this problem. Such alert doesn't impact the validity of the structure solution. 
;
_vrf_PLAT342_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K
;
PROBLEM: Low Bond Precision on  C-C Bonds ...............    0.02125 Ang.
RESPONSE: This problem is due to the thermal motion of the carbon atoms. Since we mainly focus on the analysis of the inorganic component of the structure, this alert involving organic cation will not affect our study.
;
_vrf_PLAT971_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_2
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  2.08Ang From I3              2.91 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density near the heavy atoms, which is around 5% of the electron density of I3. It is not from unaccounted atom types. Due to the phase transition and the layered nature of the structure, small densities of stacking faults or other unresolved disorder may lead to this problem. Such alert doesn't impact the validity of the structure solution. 
;
_vrf_PLAT971_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_3
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.80Ang From C4              2.77 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density around 2.42 Ang away from the heavy atom I5, which is around 5% of the electron density of I5. It is not from unaccounted atom types. Due to the phase transition and the layered nature of the structure, small densities of stacking faults or other unresolved disorder may lead to this problem. Such alert doesn't impact the validity of the structure solution.  
;
_vrf_PLAT972_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.37Ang From Pb1            -2.57 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density near the heavy atoms, which is around 2% of the electron density of Pb1. It is not from unaccounted atom types. Due to the phase transition and the layered nature of the structure, small densities of stacking faults or other unresolved disorder may lead to this problem. Such alert doesn't impact the validity of the structure solution. 
